※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4586

※ How many there are is given as an argument, so it cannot also be in the type:
※ an array type that says its length says something the count would then have to
※ agree with, and two statements of one thing can disagree.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let b: u8⟦⟧ = ⎕span(8u64, 4u64, ⌜u8⟦4⟧⌝)
    if #b = 4: 0u6 else: 1u6
